The UPSTYLE YARA rule (01-panos-globalprotect/panos_upstyle_backdoor.yar) uses
the strings and logic of Volexity's rule apt_malware_py_upstyle, published under
the BSD 2-Clause licence in github.com/volexity/threat-intel. The TINYSHELL
hunting rules credit Mandiant; the OVERSTEP hash rule uses the SHA-256 values
GTIG published. The Ivanti SPAWN-family, PHASEJAM and DRYHOOK rules
(03-ivanti-connect-secure/ivanti_spawn_family_mandiant_2025.yar) are Mandiant's,
as published by Google Threat Intelligence Group in 2025.

